speechtext:
Mr. HARRIS;
How many radio licence fees were paid in each of the following provinces:	British
Columbia, Alberta, Saskatchewan, Manitoba, Ontario, Quebec, New Brunswick, Nova Scotia and Prince Edward Island, during the years 1936 and 1937?

The minister has given figures showing that importations in the last two or three years have been very small in comparison with the amount produced in Canada.
I shall not dispute the accuracy of his figures;
I believe they are correct. However, here is the situation: The tariff was reduced once by the 1935 agreement, and our companies have been able to carry on and to maintain their position in the British market. I know of some companies whose payrolls in the last year have fallen off by nearly $100,000.
